    "title": "pandas.PeriodDtype — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.PeriodDtype#\n\n- \nclass pandas.PeriodDtype(*freq* )[source]#\n- An ExtensionDtype for Period data. **This is not an actual numpy dtype** , but a duck type.\n  - Parameters:\n    - **freq** str or DateOffset\n    - The frequency of this PeriodDtype.\n Attributes `freq`The frequency object of this PeriodDtype. See also \n  - `Period`\n  - Represents a single time period.\n  - `PeriodIndex`\n  - Immutable index for period data.\n  - `date_range`\n  - Return a fixed frequency DatetimeIndex.\n  - `Series`\n  - One-dimensional array with axis labels.\n  - `DataFrame`\n  - Two-dimensional, size-mutable, potentially heterogeneous tabular data.\n Examples >>> pd.PeriodDtype(freq=\"D\") period[D] >>> pd.PeriodDtype(freq=pd.offsets.MonthEnd()) period[M]",
